    "description": "Software developer\n•\tManage custom software applications for RoofTop and Self Contained unit controllers.  Duties included designing software, resolving issues, developing software and testing.\n•\tTest and debug RoofTop, Self Contained and chiller unit controller’s firmware applications using Siemens SAPRO and SCOPE development tools.  These versions include VVS8, VVS9, and VVS10 tools.\n•\tDevelopment, test and resolve issues with MicroTech II/III controllers, HMIs and BAS (Building Automation System) controls.  Testing included BACnet Ethernet, BACnet IP, BACnet MSTP (RS-485 network), LonWorks and MODBUS communications.  BACnet was tested to BTL (BACnet Test Laboratories) test specifications.\n•\tUse Carel OneTool to convert Chiller unit controller applications from Carel pCO3 to pCO5+.  These conversion processes include programming, functional testing and resolve issues for unit applications with BAS communications.\n•\tMaintain Unit Ventilation applications using Johnson Controls’ development tools which are FX Application, FX – UI FX-Loader and ServiceTool.\n•\tParticipated in MTIII Apply Air Handling application development using SIEMENS flatform.  This project included coding, functional testing and communication testing.  Project completed and released in 2009.  \n•\tParticipated in developing MAC unit application using Niagara Framework Programming and Tridium Technology.\n•\tUsed HTML, JavaScript to write and test codes for MicroTech II ServiceTools.\n•\tUsed Metasys Application BASIC (M-BASIC) to manage, create, develop and maintain MicroTechII RoofTop, Self Contained applications.",
